From: Grant McNaught <1371263+gmcnaught@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 18:21:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 26/49] fix(entities): invalidate ground cache when observer
 status drops (review finding)

---
 src/entities/Entity.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/entities/Entity.cpp b/src/entities/Entity.cpp
index 18e6989..65ab4df 100644
--- a/src/entities/Entity.cpp
+++ b/src/entities/Entity.cpp
@@ -239,6 +239,15 @@ void Entity::update_ground_below(bool force) {
 
   if (!is_ground_observer()) {
     // This entity does not care about the ground below it.
+    // [SOLARUS_GROUNDCACHE] is_ground_observer() can be stateful (e.g.
+    // CarriedObject only observes while being thrown; CustomEntity toggles
+    // it based on whether its Lua script currently defines
+    // on_ground_below_changed) -- invalidate so a later resumed-observing
+    // call is guaranteed to requery rather than serve a cache entry that
+    // may now be stale for reasons this entity's own movement wouldn't
+    // have caught (e.g. it moved, or a nearby modifier changed, while it
+    // wasn't observing).
+    ground_cache_valid = false;
     return;
   }
 
